low/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree"},"is_input_complete":true,"thought_signature":null}},{"ToolUse":{"id":"exec-d5ac4eec-c8b4-48aa-a6e5-afd0a2f9c5af","name":"rtk git status --short --branch","raw_input":"{\"command\":\"rtk git status --short --branch\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree\"}","input":{"command":"rtk git status --short --branch","cwd":"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree"},"is_input_complete":true,"thought_signature":null}},{"Text":"{\n \"schema_version\":1,\n \"workstream_id\": \"ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA\",\n \"run_id\": \"run-1793027022575\",\n \"node_id\": \"intake.codex_product_review\",\n \"result\": {\n \"artifact_type\": \"agent_output_contract\",\n \"decision\": \"READY_FOR_PRODUCT_REVIEW\",\n \"summary\": \"提案完整保留用户要求，计算、证据可用性和展示职责清楚，可进入后续设计与批准。\",\n \"lifecycle_status\": \"READY\",\n \"blocking\": false,\n \"checks\": [\n \"产品经理视角：逐项核对 AC-1 至 AC-5，计算口径、独立样例、异常边界、说明文档、回归证据及交付顺序均已进入约束性字段。\",\n \"架构视角：边界审查通过。PhaseOneAssessmentService 是计算和可用性判定的唯一来源，PhaseOneAssessment 承载 typed结果，CLI仅消费展示；无需新增领域模型或外部服务。\",\n \"最终用户视角：明确区分累计阈值、APR 和未来预测；不可用时保留原因，既有建议、小额验证上限和风险限制不变。\",\n \"端到端约束审查：AC-3、AC-4、C-3、C-4 声明证据不足时禁止产生和展示精确阈值；TR-2、TR-3 要求验证服务禁用与 CLI 不打印数值，失败沿既有 blockers/unknowns传递。\",\n \"权限与完成边界：六个文件条目属于候选规划，不构成写入授权；后续仍须取得精确 EXECUTION scope 批准，验收通过也不等于完整 E2E 完成。\"\n ],\n \"evidence\": [\n \"已先审阅 Review Evidence Brief，再针对固定基线、精度和成本可用性进行只读抽查；未进行逐行代码评审。\",\n \"Git 工具确认当前分支为 codex/w09-okx-break-even-20261026，HEAD 为7c5facc，工作区干净，与提案 AC-5 一致。\",\n \"PhaseOneAssessmentService.java 确认使用 MathContext.DECIMAL128、365 天年化分母和5000 USDT 首次验证上限；现有净收入比较仅在 blockers 与 unknowns 均为空时产生。\",\n \"SmartArbitrageCosts.java 确认 knownTotal() 汇总已知成本，unknowns() 单独报告缺失项。因此提案要求复用既有比较资格，能够避免仅凭已知成本合计生成误导性阈值。\",\n \"独立算术复核：20000 ×0.0365 ×90 ÷365 =180；(180 +20) ÷10000 =0.02；10000 × 累计费率 −20 −180 在三个样例点分别为 -10、0、10。\"\n ],\n \"missing_evidence\": [],\n \"must_fix\": [],\n \"contract_obligations\": [],\n \"acceptance_notes\": [\n \"本次认可的是任务提案的完整性和可验证性；未执行实现测试，也未将计划中的边界约束宣称为已强制执行或已证明闭环。\",\n \"后续设计应落实累计费率展示精度，并由服务和 CLI 测试证明不可用结果不能绕过展示限制；这些义务已由现有提案覆盖，无需扩大范围。\",\n \"节点输出封装与路由协议由 orchestrator 独立负责，不要求任务提案重复声明。\"\n ],\n \"open_risks\": [],\n \"changed_files\": [],\n \"verification_summary\": \"完成需求覆盖、边界职责、独立算例及高风险仓库事实核对，未发现阻止提案前进的问题；未修改文件或运行测试。\",\n \"failure\": {\n \"category_hint\": \"\",\n \"verification_remediation\": \"NONE\",\n \"contract_gaps\": [],\n \"out_of_scope_files\": [],\n \"missing_tests\": [],\n \"context_gaps\": [],\n \"reason\": \"\"\n },\n \"reread_reasons\": []\n }\n}"}],"tool_results":{"exec-3bcee483-2c8b-45cd-94a6-cbfbbed74c4e":{"tool_use_id":"exec-3bcee483-2c8b-45cd-94a6-cbfbbed74c4e","tool_name":"rtk read /Users/kriswang/.codex/skills/boundary-first-engineering/SKILL.md","is_error":false,"content":{"Text":"{\"formatted_output\":\"---\\nname: boundary-first-engineering\\ndescription: Use before changing or reviewing systems with non-trivial state, lifecycle transitions, workflow/orchestration, external adapters, retries, recovery, compensation, async workers, queues, schedulers, human decisions, structured contracts, events, ledgers, projections, dashboards, reports, UI/CLI/API status, or completion semantics. Trigger when symptoms include repeated local fixes, ambiguous completion, stale running state, duplicated status logic, natural-language parsing drift, hidden evidence, projection disagreement, retry/resume confusion, terminal-state leaks, or any temptation to fix a state bug with handler-local if/else.\\n---\\n\\n# Boundary-First Engineering\\n\\nUse this skill as a state-boundary discipline, not as a project-specific checklist. The goal is to prevent local patches from bypassing domain boundaries.\\n\\n## First Move\\n\\nBefore editing code, state the suspected boundary:\\n\\n- Domain state / lifecycle model\\n- Definition / instance / execution model\\n- External adapter / activity boundary\\n- Structured artifact / event / command contract\\n- Retry / recovery / compensation semantics\\n- Human decision / approval semantics\\n- Completion / terminal-state contract\\n- Projection / UI / CLI / API / report read model\\n\\nIf the boundary is unclear, inspect the model, source of truth, and data flow first. Do not start with DOM tweaks, substring rules, handler-local branches, or projection fixes.\\n\\n\\n## Automatic Boundary Loop\\n\\nFor any boundary-sensitive task, run this loop until the material boundary findings are resolved or explicitly accepted as debt:\\n\\n```text\\nAnalyze -> Modify -> Review -> Reflect -> Analyze\\n```\\n\\n- Analyze: name the boundary, source of truth, affected projections, and expected invariant before editing.\\n- Modify: change the source-of-truth model or typed boundary first; update projections after.\\n- Review: re-run this skill against the diff and classify findings as PASS / WARN / FAIL.\\n- Reflect: record why the issue happened, whether the model/discipline missed a trigger, and what test or rule prevents recurrence.\\n- Re-enter Analyze when Review is WARN/FAIL, when a fix introduces a new boundary, or when the reasoning relied on a stopgap.\\n\\nDo not treat a stateful fix as complete after one green test if the Review or Reflect step exposes an unguarded boundary.\\n\\n## Model Ownership Check\\n\\nReplay the existing model before proposing or editing stateful code:\\n\\n```text\\nExisting model:\\n- Definition: what is declared or configured?\\n- Instance: what durable business/process occurrence exists?\\n- Execution: what concrete run/attempt/process happened?\\n- Event / Ledger / History: what facts are recorded and replayable?\\n- Artifact / Contract: what structured output is trusted?\\n- Human Decision: what did a person decide, and at which gate?\\n- Projection: what is read-only display or reporting?\\n\\nProblem ownership:\\n- Which existing object should own this fact or transition?\\n\\nNew concept needed:\\n- No / Yes. If yes, why can no existing object carry it?\\n```\\n\\nRules:\\n\\n- Prefer established domain terms. Do not invent synonyms such as attempt, run, job, task, stage, or checkpoint if definition / instance / execution / event / artifact / gate already fits.\\n- Execution owns runtime facts: pid, command, stdout, stderr, exit code, timeout, interruption, stale process, retry evidence, and external tool failures.\\n- Instance owns the durable occurrence of a process, node, order, job, request, workflow, or business lifecycle.\\n- Iteration or revision owns semantic rework. Runtime retry is not semantic iteration.\\n- Goal or business aggregate owns user intent and satisfaction truth. Workflow completion alone is not goal satisfaction.\\n- Projection owns display only. UI, CLI, dashboards, summaries, and reports must not invent state.\\n\\n## Source Of Truth\\n\\nIdentify one authoritative source before changing behavior:\\n\\n-..."},"output":{"formatted_output":"---\nname: boundary-first-engineering\ndescription: Use before changing or reviewing systems with non-trivial state, lifecycle transitions, workflow/orchestration, external adapters, retries, recovery, compensation, async workers, queues, schedulers, human decisions, structured contracts, events, ledgers, projections, dashboards, reports, UI/CLI/API status, or completion semantics. Trigger when symptoms include repeated local fixes, ambiguous completion, stale running state, duplicated status logic, natural-language parsing drift, hidden evidence, projection disagreement, retry/resume confusion, terminal-state leaks, or any temptation to fix a state bug with handler-local if/else.\n---\n\n# Boundary-First Engineering\n\nUse this skill as a state-boundary discipline, not as a project-specific checklist. The goal is to prevent local patches from bypassing domain boundaries.\n\n## First Move\n\nBefore editing code, state the suspected boundary:\n\n- Domain state / lifecycle model\n- Definition / instance / execution model\n- External adapter / activity boundary\n- Structured artifact / event / command contract\n- Retry / recovery / compensation semantics\n- Human decision / approval semantics\n- Completion / terminal-state contract\n- Projection / UI / CLI / API / report read model\n\nIf the boundary is unclear, inspect the model, source of truth, and data flow first. Do not start with DOM tweaks, substring rules, handler-local branches, or projection fixes.\n\n\n## Automatic Boundary Loop\n\nFor any boundary-sensitive task, run this loop until the material boundary findings are resolved or explicitly accepted as debt:\n\n```text\nAnalyze -> Modify -> Review -> Reflect -> Analyze\n```\n\n- Analyze: name the boundary, source of truth, affected projections, and expected invariant before editing.\n- Modify: change the source-of-truth model or typed boundary first; update projections after.\n- Review: re-run this skill against the diff and classify findings as PASS / WARN / FAIL.\n- Reflect: record why the issue happened, whether the model/discipline missed a trigger, and what test or rule prevents recurrence.\n- Re-enter Analyze when Review is WARN/FAIL, when a fix introduces a new boundary, or when the reasoning relied on a stopgap.\n\nDo not treat a stateful fix as complete after one green test if the Review or Reflect step exposes an unguarded boundary.\n\n## Model Ownership Check\n\nReplay the existing model before proposing or editing stateful code:\n\n```text\nExisting model:\n- Definition: what is declared or configured?\n- Instance: what durable business/process occurrence exists?\n- Execution: what concrete run/attempt/process happened?\n- Event / Ledger / History: what facts are recorded and replayable?\n- Artifact / Contract: what structured output is trusted?\n- Human Decision: what did a person decide, and at which gate?\n- Projection: what is read-only display or reporting?\n\nProblem ownership:\n- Which existing object should own this fact or transition?\n\nNew concept needed:\n- No / Yes. If yes, why can no existing object carry it?\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- Prefer established domain terms. Do not invent synonyms such as attempt, run, job, task, stage, or checkpoint if definition / instance / execution / event / artifact / gate already fits.\n- Execution owns runtime facts: pid, command, stdout, stderr, exit code, timeout, interruption, stale process, retry evidence, and external tool failures.\n- Instance owns the durable occurrence of a process, node, order, job, request, workflow, or business lifecycle.\n- Iteration or revision owns semantic rework. Runtime retry is not semantic iteration.\n- Goal or business aggregate owns user intent and satisfaction truth. Workflow completion alone is not goal satisfaction.\n- Projection owns display only. UI, CLI, dashboards, summaries, and reports must not invent state.\n\n## Source Of Truth\n\nIdentify one authoritative source before changing behavior:\n\n- Domain object or aggregate for business truth.\n- Event history / ledger for how the state was reached.\n- Structured artifact / schema for LLM or external output.\n- Adapter metadata for external runtime failures.\n- Read model only for projection.\n\nIf the same status, next action, or decision is computed in UI, CLI, API, and runtime separately, stop and centralize it behind a semantic read model.\n\n## Sibling Boundary Sweep\n\nWhen a fix removes or relocates a source of truth, do not stop at the first failing symbol or the first user-mentioned method. Search for sibling concepts that share the same boundary.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Removing one workflow variant generated by Java means checking every built-in variant, not only the one named in the bug.\n- Moving one lifecycle definition to JSON means checking all lifecycle definition sources, docs, tests, CLI options, smoke cases, and generated examples.\n- Centralizing one projection field means checking every UI / CLI / API / report surface that answers the same user question.\n\nRequired sweep before completion:\n\n```text\nPrimary concept changed:\nSibling concepts with the same owner:\nAuthoritative source after the change:\nOld source paths removed:\nTests that protect the new boundary:\nResidual compatibility kept:\nWhy the residual compatibility is necessary:\n```\n\nIf residual compatibility is not necessary, delete it. If it is kept, document the owner, expiry condition, and test coverage. Do not keep a legacy path just because it still passes.\n\n## Definition / Registry Drift Sweep\n\nWhen a system has declarative definitions plus code registries, treat drift as a boundary risk, not a simple missing entry.\n\nCheck these pairs together:\n\n- Workflow / lifecycle definition vs runtime factory or handler registry.\n- Node ids and edge outcomes vs artifact/output contract registry.\n- Failure reason catalog vs recovery assessment and operator next actions.\n- Gate metadata / allowed actions vs CLI, API, UI, and autorun actions.\n- Read model / projection semantics vs UI, CLI, API, reports, and dashboards.\n\nRules:\n\n- A registry is acceptable only as a named boundary: capability catalog, failure signal catalog, contract validator, or projection policy.\n- A registry is not acceptable when it silently becomes a second workflow definition or a second state machine.\n- When adding or fixing one registry entry, add a consistency test against the authoritative definition.\n- Do not preserve old registry paths unless real users need compatibility; if kept, state the owner and expiry condition.\n- If declarative config and code disagree, fix the source-of-truth boundary first, then update projections.\n\nRequired drift check:\n\n```text\nAuthoritative definition:\nCode registry/catalog touching the same concept:\nCan the registry derive from the definition?\nConsistency test added:\nResidual hardcode kept:\nWhy the hardcode is a named boundary rather than drift:\n```\n\n## External Adapter Rule\n\nTreat LLMs, CLIs, network APIs, databases, queues, file I/O, and tools as external activities/adapters:\n\n- Record their inputs, outputs, exit status, duration, and failure category.\n- Do not let natural-language text directly mutate domain state.\n- Convert external output into a typed artifact, event, or failure signal first.\n- Classify adapter failures separately from business rejection.\n- Keep provider-specific wording in an adapter catalog or parser, not in workflow or UI code.\n\n## Transition And Terminal Rules\n\n- Core runtime must guard terminal states before creating new execution records or side effects.\n- Terminal states may allow observation, summary, export, or audit; they must not allow run/resume/retry/approve unless the domain explicitly defines a reopening command.\n- Guards must be side-effect free. Actions that mutate state belong in transition handlers or domain methods.\n- Retry handles recoverable execution failure. Repair handles unmet business goal. Compensation closes or offsets an already-taken wrong action. Do not mix them.\n- If an error is terminal/non-retriable, model it explicitly instead of hiding it behind a catch-all retry.\n\n## Human Decision Rules\n\n- Human gates must expose allowed actions, evidence, recommendation, and consequences.\n- Current gates may expose actions. Historical gates are read-only evidence.\n- Human review should judge product/domain evidence, not compensate for unclear workflow mechanics.\n- Gate purpose should come from metadata or domain model. Node-id fallback is acceptable only as isolated legacy compatibility.\n\n## Projection Rules\n\n- Define the user question first: where is it, why did it stop, what evidence supports this, what action is allowed next, or what happened historically?\n- Put object-specific evidence before shared context.\n- Current-state panels and historical evidence panels must be different modes.\n- If multiple cards/items look identical, the projection is wrong even if the data is technically present.\n- UI, CLI, API, reports, and dashboards should consume the same read model for status, attention, next action, and completion.\n\n## Red Flags\n\nPause and redo the ownership check when you see:\n\n- A fix that is mostly another contains/startsWith branch.\n- A source-of-truth migration that fixes one variant, mode, command, or projection while leaving siblings on the old mechanism.\n- A terminal object that can still be resumed or approved.\n- Runtime failure recorded as business failure.\n- Semantic repair recorded as runtime retry.\n- Natural-language parsing used as the primary decision source.\n- UI says one status while CLI/API/ledger says another.\n- Projection code scanning files and deriving lifecycle decisions independently.\n- Human review needed to validate flow mechanics rather than domain evidence.\n- A new field added to one surface but not to the authoritative model.\n- A registry or factory that repeats workflow nodes, edge outcomes, handler types, or output contracts without a consistency test.\n- A real-case failure that is fixed by adding one more string branch without sweeping sibling reasons, states, projections, and registries.\n\n## Stopgap Admission\n\nUse a stopgap only when the system is blocked and a model fix is too costly right now. Label it explicitly:\n\n```text\nStopgap fix:\n- What is contained:\n- Why this is not the final model:\n- Why it does not corrupt the source of truth:\n- Follow-up model fix:\n- Revisit trigger:\n```\n\nDo not call a stopgap a lifecycle closure.\n\n## Required Review Output\n\nFor design or review tasks, report:\n\n```text\nBoundary Review: PASS / WARN / FAIL\nTouched boundaries:\nSource of truth:\nProjection surfaces:\nFindings:\nRequired fixes:\nRequired tests:\nAccepted debt, if any:\n```\n\nFor implementation tasks, keep this review internal while working, then summarize only the material findings and verification evidence.\n\n## Completion Criteria\n\nA stateful change is not complete until:\n\n- The source-of-truth boundary is named and preserved.\n- Definition / instance / execution are not conflated.\n- External adapter results are converted to typed facts before routing.\n- Terminal states are guarded in core logic, not only UI/API.\n- Projection does not invent lifecycle state.\n- Current and historical semantics are separated.\n- Retry, repair, and compensation are distinct.\n- At least one boundary test or realistic check covers the risky transition.\n","exit_code":0}},"exec-0b34a5e4-12e7-495d-8069-8397a39f734b":{"tool_use_id":"exec-0b34a5e4-12e7-495d-8069-8397a39f734b","tool_name":"rtk read src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/application/PhaseOneAssessmentService.java","is_error":false,"content":{"Text":"{\"formatted_output\":\"package app.cryptoincome.assessment.application;\\n\\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.EvidenceStatus;\\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.FundingHistoryEvidence;\\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.FundingRatePoint;\\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.PhaseOneAssessment;\\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.PhaseOneAssessmentRequest;\\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.Recommendation;\\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.TerminalPolicy;\\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Service;\\n\\nimport java.math.BigDecimal;\\nimport java.math.MathContext;\\nimport java.time.Instant;\\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\\nimport java.util.Comparator;\\nimport java.util.List;\\nimport java.util.Optional;\\n\\n@Service\\npublic class PhaseOneAssessmentService {\\n\\n    private static final MathContext CALCULATION_CONTEXT = MathContext.DECIMAL128;\\n    private static final BigDecimal DAYS_PER_YEAR = new BigDecimal(\\\"365\\\");\\n    private static final BigDecimal MAXIMUM_FIRST_LIVE_CAPITAL = new BigDecimal(\\\"5000\\\");\\n    private static final String EXCHANGE = \\\"OKX\\\";\\n    private static final String INSTRUMENT = \\\"BTC-USDT-SWAP\\\";\\n\\n    private final FundingRateFactQuery fundingRateFactQuery;\\n\\n    public PhaseOneAssessmentService(FundingRateFactQuery fundingRateFactQuery) {\\n        this.fundingRateFactQuery = fundingRateFactQuery;\\n    }\\n\\n    public PhaseOneAssessment assess(PhaseOneAssessmentRequest request) {\\n        List<FundingRatePoint> points = fundingRateFactQuery.findRealizedRates(\\n                EXCHANGE, INSTRUMENT, request.from(), request.to(), request.evaluationAsOf());\\n        List<FundingRatePoint> ordered = points.stream()\\n                .sorted(Comparator.comparing(FundingRatePoint::fundingTime))\\n                .toList();\\n\\n        BigDecimal holdingReturn = ordered.stream()\\n                .map(FundingRatePoint::realizedRate)\\n                .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);\\n        BigDecimal fundingIncome = request.hedgedShortNotional().multiply(holdingReturn);\\n        BigDecimal simpleEarnIncome = request.candidateCapital()\\n                .multiply(request.simpleEarnQuote().apr())\\n                .multiply(new BigDecimal(request.simpleEarnQuote().termDays()))\\n                .divide(DAYS_PER_YEAR, CALCULATION_CONTEXT);\\n        BigDecimal knownCost = request.costs().knownTotal();\\n\\n        FundingHistoryEvidence history = new FundingHistoryEvidence(\\n                holdingReturn,\\n                fundingIncome,\\n                ordered.size(),\\n                (int) ordered.stream().filter(point -> point.realizedRate().signum() > 0).count(),\\n                (int) ordered.stream().filter(point -> point.realizedRate().signum() < 0).count(),\\n                ordered.stream().map(FundingRatePoint::fundingTime).min(Instant::compareTo),\\n                ordered.stream().map(FundingRatePoint::fundingTime).max(Instant::compareTo));\\n\\n        List<String> blockers = new ArrayList<>();\\n        List<String> unknowns = new ArrayList<>(request.costs().unknowns());\\n        List<String> reasons = new ArrayList<>();\\n        Optional<BigDecimal> netIncome = Optional.empty();\\n        Optional<BigDecimal> incremental = Optional.empty();\\n        EvidenceStatus evidenceStatus;\\n        Recommendation recommendation;\\n\\n        if (!request.simpleEarnQuote().termsConfirmed()) {\\n            blockers.add(\\\"简单赚币确认页条款尚未人工确认\\\");\\n        }\\n        if (ordered.isEmpty()) {\\n            blockers.add(\\\"90 天窗口内没有可用的已实现资金费率事实\\\");\\n        }\\n        if (request.terminalPolicy() == TerminalPolicy.KEEP_STRATEGY_OPEN) {\\n            unknowns.add(\\\"期末未退出，无法与到期回到 USDT 的简单赚币同口径比较\\\");\\n        }\\n\\n        if (!blockers.isEmpty()) {\\n            evidenceStatus = EvidenceStatus.INSUFFICIENT;\\n            recommendation = Recommendation.INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE;\\n            reasons.addAll(blockers);\\n        } else if (!unknowns.isEmpty()) {\\n            evidenceStat..."},"output":{"formatted_output":"package app.cryptoincome.assessment.application;\n\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.EvidenceStatus;\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.FundingHistoryEvidence;\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.FundingRatePoint;\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.PhaseOneAssessment;\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.PhaseOneAssessmentRequest;\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.Recommendation;\nimport app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain.TerminalPolicy;\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Service;\n\nimport java.math.BigDecimal;\nimport java.math.MathContext;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Comparator;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Optional;\n\n@Service\npublic class PhaseOneAssessmentService {\n\n    private static final MathContext CALCULATION_CONTEXT = MathContext.DECIMAL128;\n    private static final BigDecimal DAYS_PER_YEAR = new BigDecimal(\"365\");\n    private static final BigDecimal MAXIMUM_FIRST_LIVE_CAPITAL = new BigDecimal(\"5000\");\n    private static final String EXCHANGE = \"OKX\";\n    private static final String INSTRUMENT = \"BTC-USDT-SWAP\";\n\n    private final FundingRateFactQuery fundingRateFactQuery;\n\n    public PhaseOneAssessmentService(FundingRateFactQuery fundingRateFactQuery) {\n        this.fundingRateFactQuery = fundingRateFactQuery;\n    }\n\n    public PhaseOneAssessment assess(PhaseOneAssessmentRequest request) {\n        List<FundingRatePoint> points = fundingRateFactQuery.findRealizedRates(\n                EXCHANGE, INSTRUMENT, request.from(), request.to(), request.evaluationAsOf());\n        List<FundingRatePoint> ordered = points.stream()\n                .sorted(Comparator.comparing(FundingRatePoint::fundingTime))\n                .toList();\n\n        BigDecimal holdingReturn = ordered.stream()\n                .map(FundingRatePoint::realizedRate)\n                .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);\n        BigDecimal fundingIncome = request.hedgedShortNotional().multiply(holdingReturn);\n        BigDecimal simpleEarnIncome = request.candidateCapital()\n                .multiply(request.simpleEarnQuote().apr())\n                .multiply(new BigDecimal(request.simpleEarnQuote().termDays()))\n                .divide(DAYS_PER_YEAR, CALCULATION_CONTEXT);\n        BigDecimal knownCost = request.costs().knownTotal();\n\n        FundingHistoryEvidence history = new FundingHistoryEvidence(\n                holdingReturn,\n                fundingIncome,\n                ordered.size(),\n                (int) ordered.stream().filter(point -> point.realizedRate().signum() > 0).count(),\n                (int) ordered.stream().filter(point -> point.realizedRate().signum() < 0).count(),\n                ordered.stream().map(FundingRatePoint::fundingTime).min(Instant::compareTo),\n                ordered.stream().map(FundingRatePoint::fundingTime).max(Instant::compareTo));\n\n        List<String> blockers = new ArrayList<>();\n        List<String> unknowns = new ArrayList<>(request.costs().unknowns());\n        List<String> reasons = new ArrayList<>();\n        Optional<BigDecimal> netIncome = Optional.empty();\n        Optional<BigDecimal> incremental = Optional.empty();\n        EvidenceStatus evidenceStatus;\n        Recommendation recommendation;\n\n        if (!request.simpleEarnQuote().termsConfirmed()) {\n            blockers.add(\"简单赚币确认页条款尚未人工确认\");\n        }\n        if (ordered.isEmpty()) {\n            blockers.add(\"90 天窗口内没有可用的已实现资金费率事实\");\n        }\n        if (request.terminalPolicy() == TerminalPolicy.KEEP_STRATEGY_OPEN) {\n            unknowns.add(\"期末未退出，无法与到期回到 USDT 的简单赚币同口径比较\");\n        }\n\n        if (!blockers.isEmpty()) {\n            evidenceStatus = EvidenceStatus.INSUFFICIENT;\n            recommendation = Recommendation.INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE;\n            reasons.addAll(blockers);\n        } else if (!unknowns.isEmpty()) {\n            evidenceStatus = EvidenceStatus.INSUFFICIENT;\n            recommendation = Recommendation.WATCH_SMART_ARBITRAGE;\n            reasons.add(\"关键成本或期末状态仍未知，不能把未知按 0 计算\");\n        } else {\n            BigDecimal net = fundingIncome.subtract(knownCost);\n            BigDecimal delta = net.subtract(simpleEarnIncome);\n            netIncome = Optional.of(net);\n            incremental = Optional.of(delta);\n            if (delta.signum() <= 0) {\n                evidenceStatus = EvidenceStatus.SUFFICIENT_FOR_COMPARISON;\n                recommendation = Recommendation.PREFER_SIMPLE_EARN;\n                reasons.add(\"资金费率收入扣除完整已知成本后不高于 90 天简单赚币\");\n            } else {\n                evidenceStatus = EvidenceStatus.SUFFICIENT_FOR_MICRO_VALIDATION;\n                recommendation = Recommendation.MICRO_VALIDATE_ARBITRAGE;\n                reasons.add(\"历史情景扣除完整已知成本后高于简单赚币，但尚无真实闭环\");\n            }\n        }\n\n        List<String> checklist = recommendation == Recommendation.MICRO_VALIDATE_ARBITRAGE\n                ? List.of(\n                        \"重新核对 OKX 90 天简单赚币 APR、额度和赎回条款\",\n                        \"重新打开 BTC-USDT 智能套利预览并核对两腿名义和预计开仓成本\",\n                        \"首次只投入 2,000–5,000 USDT\",\n                        \"保存实际成交、资金费、再平衡和退出费用\",\n                        \"退出回 USDT 后复盘预计与实际差异\")\n                : List.of();\n\n        return new PhaseOneAssessment(\n                request, simpleEarnIncome, history, knownCost, netIncome, incremental,\n                evidenceStatus, recommendation,\n                recommendation == Recommendation.MICRO_VALIDATE_ARBITRAGE\n                        ? Optional.of(MAXIMUM_FIRST_LIVE_CAPITAL) : Optional.empty(),\n                reasons, blockers, unknowns, checklist);\n    }\n}\n","exit_code":0}},"exec-4e6f2b8f-7384-442c-aaba-5f6101b72fba":{"tool_use_id":"exec-4e6f2b8f-7384-442c-aaba-5f6101b72fba","tool_name":"rtk read src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/domain/SmartArbitrageCosts.java","is_error":false,"content":{"Text":"{\"formatted_output\":\"package app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain;\\n\\nimport java.math.BigDecimal;\\nimport java.time.Instant;\\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\\nimport java.util.List;\\nimport java.util.Objects;\\nimport java.util.Optional;\\n\\npublic record SmartArbitrageCosts(\\n        Instant asOf,\\n        String source,\\n        Optional<OpeningCost> openingCost,\\n        Optional<BigDecimal> exitCost,\\n        Optional<BigDecimal> slippageCost,\\n        Optional<BigDecimal> rebalanceCost,\\n        Optional<BigDecimal> serviceCost\\n) {\\n    public SmartArbitrageCosts {\\n        Objects.requireNonNull(asOf, \\\"asOf 不能为空\\\");\\n        if (source == null || source.isBlank()) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\\\"source 不能为空\\\");\\n        openingCost = Objects.requireNonNull(openingCost, \\\"openingCost 不能为空\\\");\\n        exitCost = requireOptionalCost(exitCost, \\\"退出成本\\\");\\n        slippageCost = requireOptionalCost(slippageCost, \\\"滑点成本\\\");\\n        rebalanceCost = requireOptionalCost(rebalanceCost, \\\"再平衡成本\\\");\\n        serviceCost = requireOptionalCost(serviceCost, \\\"服务/融资成本\\\");\\n    }\\n\\n    public BigDecimal knownTotal() {\\n        BigDecimal total = openingCost.map(OpeningCost::amount).orElse(BigDecimal.ZERO);\\n        return total.add(exitCost.orElse(BigDecimal.ZERO))\\n                .add(slippageCost.orElse(BigDecimal.ZERO))\\n                .add(rebalanceCost.orElse(BigDecimal.ZERO))\\n                .add(serviceCost.orElse(BigDecimal.ZERO));\\n    }\\n\\n    public boolean complete() {\\n        return openingCost.isPresent() && exitCost.isPresent() && slippageCost.isPresent()\\n                && rebalanceCost.isPresent() && serviceCost.isPresent();\\n    }\\n\\n    public List<String> unknowns() {\\n        List<String> result = new ArrayList<>();\\n        if (openingCost.isEmpty()) result.add(\\\"开仓成本\\\");\\n        if (exitCost.isEmpty()) result.add(\\\"退出成本\\\");\\n        if (slippageCost.isEmpty()) result.add(\\\"滑点成本\\\");\\n        if (rebalanceCost.isEmpty()) result.add(\\\"再平衡成本\\\");\\n        if (serviceCost.isEmpty()) result.add(\\\"服务/融资成本\\\");\\n        return List.copyOf(result);\\n    }\\n\\n    private static Optional<BigDecimal> requireOptionalCost(Optional<BigDecimal> value, String name) {\\n        Objects.requireNonNull(value, name + \\\"不能为空\\\");\\n        value.ifPresent(cost -> {\\n            if (cost.signum() < 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(name + \\\"不能为负数\\\");\\n        });\\n        return value;\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0}"},"output":{"formatted_output":"package app.cryptoincome.assessment.domain;\n\nimport java.math.BigDecimal;\nimport java.time.Instant;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\nimport java.util.Objects;\nimport java.util.Optional;\n\npublic record SmartArbitrageCosts(\n        Instant asOf,\n        String source,\n        Optional<OpeningCost> openingCost,\n        Optional<BigDecimal> exitCost,\n        Optional<BigDecimal> slippageCost,\n        Optional<BigDecimal> rebalanceCost,\n        Optional<BigDecimal> serviceCost\n) {\n    public SmartArbitrageCosts {\n        Objects.requireNonNull(asOf, \"asOf 不能为空\");\n        if (source == null || source.isBlank()) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"source 不能为空\");\n        openingCost = Objects.requireNonNull(openingCost, \"openingCost 不能为空\");\n        exitCost = requireOptionalCost(exitCost, \"退出成本\");\n        slippageCost = requireOptionalCost(slippageCost, \"滑点成本\");\n        rebalanceCost = requireOptionalCost(rebalanceCost, \"再平衡成本\");\n        serviceCost = requireOptionalCost(serviceCost, \"服务/融资成本\");\n    }\n\n    public BigDecimal knownTotal() {\n        BigDecimal total = openingCost.map(OpeningCost::amount).orElse(BigDecimal.ZERO);\n        return total.add(exitCost.orElse(BigDecimal.ZERO))\n                .add(slippageCost.orElse(BigDecimal.ZERO))\n                .add(rebalanceCost.orElse(BigDecimal.ZERO))\n                .add(serviceCost.orElse(BigDecimal.ZERO));\n    }\n\n    public boolean complete() {\n        return openingCost.isPresent() && exitCost.isPresent() && slippageCost.isPresent()\n                && rebalanceCost.isPresent() && serviceCost.isPresent();\n    }\n\n    public List<String> unknowns() {\n        List<String> result = new ArrayList<>();\n        if (openingCost.isEmpty()) result.add(\"开仓成本\");\n        if (exitCost.isEmpty()) result.add(\"退出成本\");\n        if (slippageCost.isEmpty()) result.add(\"滑点成本\");\n        if (rebalanceCost.isEmpty()) result.add(\"再平衡成本\");\n        if (serviceCost.isEmpty()) result.add(\"服务/融资成本\");\n        return List.copyOf(result);\n    }\n\n    private static Optional<BigDecimal> requireOptionalCost(Optional<BigDecimal> value, String name) {\n        Objects.requireNonNull(value, name + \"不能为空\");\n        value.ifPresent(cost -> {\n            if (cost.signum() < 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(name + \"不能为负数\");\n        });\n        return value;\n    }\n}\n","exit_code":0}},"exec-16a5d84f-7c9f-42d7-9d40-c5a3cdcac6f9":{"tool_use_id":"exec-16a5d84f-7c9f-42d7-9d40-c5a3cdcac6f9","tool_name":"rtk git rev-parse --short HEAD","is_error":false,"content":{"Text":"{\"formatted_output\":\"7c5facc\\n\",\"exit_code\":0}"},"output":{"formatted_output":"7c5facc\n","exit_code":0}},"exec-d5ac4eec-c8b4-48aa-a6e5-afd0a2f9c5af":{"tool_use_id":"exec-d5ac4eec-c8b4-48aa-a6e5-afd0a2f9c5af","tool_name":"rtk git status --short --branch","is_error":false,"content":{"Text":"{\"formatted_output\":\"* codex/w09-okx-break-even-20261026\\nclean — nothing to commit\\n\",\"exit_code\":0}"},"output":{"formatted_output":"* codex/w09-okx-break-even-20261026\nclean — nothing to commit\n","exit_code":0}}}}}],"updated_at":"2026-10-26T15:05:21.951Z","cumulative_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2477,"output_tokens":1195,"cache_read_input_tokens":31488,"thought_tokens":231,"total_tokens":35160},"request_token_usage":{"c946d185-ba9d-476d-ad35-acb38a196010":{"input_tokens":2477,"output_tokens":1195,"cache_read_input_tokens":31488,"thought_tokens":231,"total_tokens":35160}},"acpx":{"current_model_id":"gpt-6-astra","available_models":["gpt-6-astra","gpt-5.6-sol","gpt-5.6-terra","gpt-5.6-luna"],"model_control":"config_option","config_options":[{"id":"mode","name":"Mode","description":"Approval and sandboxing preset for the session","category":"mode","type":"select","currentValue":"agent","options":[{"value":"read-only","name":"Ask for approval","description":"Always ask to edit external files and use the internet","_meta":{"kind":"standard"}},{"value":"agent","name":"Approve for me","description":"Only ask for actions detected as potentially unsafe","_meta":{"kind":"auto_review"}},{"value":"agent-full-access","name":"Full access","description":"Unrestricted access to the internet and any file on your computer","_meta":{"kind":"full_access"}}]},{"id":"collaboration_mode","name":"Collaboration mode","description":"How Codex collaborates for subsequent turns","cat